# UI copy — no guide text

## Default

Do **not** put instructions, tips, “how to use”, or explanatory essays on the UI.

Users learn from labels, layout, and affordances — not paragraphs of help.

## When copy is allowed

Only if missing it causes real mistakes (money, publish/draft, irreversible delete, legal).

Then: **shortest possible** — prefer a few words on the control itself, not a sentence under every field.

```text
❌ Full story for the product page — headings, lists… Click in text — pink button…
❌ Draft stays off Soft Gift until you Publish (repeated under Save)
✅ Label: "Product page content"
✅ Button: "Save as draft" / "Publish" (the action is the instruction)
```

## Prefer

| Instead of | Use |
|---|---|
| Hint under every section | Clear section title |
| “Optional — leave blank to…” | Placeholder on the input |
| Multi-line how-to | Nothing, or one short `title`/`aria-label` |
| Style explainer chip text | Show style chip **only when cursor is in content** |

## Do not

- Add onboarding prose to ship a feature
- Duplicate the same tip in header + toolbar + footer
- Use “lol” or chatty copy in product UI
